{ options: [ { value: '', text: 'Choose an example…' }, { value: '0', text: '1. Full table scan' }, { value: '1', text: '2. Rowid primary key lookup' }, { value: '2', text: '3. Index equality search' }, { value: '3', text: '4. Index range scan' }, { value: '4', text: '5. Covering index' }, { value: '5', text: '6. Multi-column index' }, { value: '6', text: '7. Nested loop join (three tables)' }, { value: '7', text: '8. LEFT JOIN' }, { value: '8', text: '9. ORDER BY needing a sort' }, { value: '9', text: '10. ORDER BY satisfied by an index' }, { value: '10', text: '11. GROUP BY needing a temp b-tree' }, { value: '11', text: '12. DISTINCT via covering index' }, { value: '12', text: '13. IN (subquery) — list subquery' }, { value: '13', text: '14. Correlated scalar subquery' }, { value: '14', text: '15. EXISTS subquery' }, { value: '15', text: '16. UNION vs UNION ALL' }, { value: '16', text: '17. OR using two indexes (MULTI-INDEX OR)' }, { value: '17', text: '18. Automatic index' }, { value: '18', text: '19. CTE: MATERIALIZED vs co-routine' }, { value: '19', text: '20. Recursive CTE' }, { value: '20', text: '21. Query against a view' }, { value: '21', text: '22. Window function' } ], status: [ 'SQLite has to visit all 50,000 rows and test each one.', 'SQLite chose for this query. Indented items run inside their parent; sibling loops form nested joins, with each row from an outer loop driving a full pass of the loops below it.', 'SQLite visits every row in the table and tests it against the WHERE clause. Cost grows linearly with table size — fine for small tables, but on big tables this is the classic sign that an index could help.', 'SQLite compiles every statement into a program for its virtual machine (the VDBE); this is that program, one instruction per row. The | bars mark loop bodies. Instruction numbers are links — click one to jump to it, and the ↖ from n badge on an instruction shows which other instructions jump to it. Hover a register like r[3] or a cursor to highlight everywhere else it is used.', "SQLite's handles for walking tables and indexes.", 'SQLite docs for EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN and VDBE opcodes. More tools at tools.simonwillison.net.' ], sections: [ { tag: 'DIV', id: 'status' }, { tag: 'DIV', id: 'query-card' }, { tag: 'TEXTAREA', id: 'sql' }, { tag: 'P', id: 'results-meta' }, { tag: 'TABLE', id: 'results-table' } ] }

